            <ArticleTitle>The role of cytokines in cardiovascular disease in menopause.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>524-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/13697137.2012.700743</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Various studies suggest that increased levels of pro-inflammatory cytokines play a key role in the declining ovarian function and the resulting complications associated with menopause. In this review article, the authors outline the role of pro- and anti-inflammatory cytokines in cardiovascular disease during menopause.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
